WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.982
Deception can have many goals, but from a defensive perspective the goals often cluster into a few useful categories.

2
00:00:07.982 --> 00:00:15.123
Some activity is meant to create urgency: act now, approve now, share now, disable the control now.

3
00:00:15.123 --> 00:00:23.525
Some is meant to create confusion, making the team spend time on the wrong claim or argue over incomplete context.

4
00:00:23.525 --> 00:00:32.767
Some is meant to hide source, intent, or responsibility, so that a request, artifact, or narrative appears more trustworthy than it is.

5
00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.867
Defensive signals are not proof.

6
00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:37.808
They are reasons to apply more care.

7
00:00:37.808 --> 00:00:47.890
Missing provenance, unusual urgency, unexplained gaps, selective screenshots, conflicting timestamps, and pressure to bypass normal process should all change how an analyst handles the

8
00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:48.310
claim.

9
00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.671
A single indicator may have an innocent explanation.

10
00:00:51.671 --> 00:00:56.292
A pattern of indicators may justify escalation, preservation, and independent corroboration.

11
00:00:56.292 --> 00:00:58.392
Selective evidence is especially important.

12
00:00:58.392 --> 00:01:00.913
A message thread can be cropped.

13
00:01:00.913 --> 00:01:04.694
A log line can be separated from surrounding events.

14
00:01:04.694 --> 00:01:12.676
A domain, file hash, username, or ticket number can be real while the conclusion attached to it is wrong.

15
00:01:12.676 --> 00:01:22.758
The analyst should ask what is missing, what system of record can confirm the artifact, and whether the presented evidence supports the exact claim

16
00:01:22.758 --> 00:01:25.698
or only a weaker version of it.

17
00:01:25.698 --> 00:01:31.159
The purpose of naming signals is not to make teams suspicious of everything.

18
00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:37.041
It is to give them a repeatable way to move from reaction to verification.

19
00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:41.242
When urgency is high, process becomes more valuable, not less.

20
00:01:41.242 --> 00:01:50.063
Trusted channels, approval workflows, documented assumptions, and clear escalation paths help teams make timely decisions without giving pressure the steering wheel.
